{
  "borough": "Wandsworth",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed development, by reason of its scale, design and siting, constitutes an unneighbourly form of development that harms the amenity of the neighbouring occupiers in the form of loss outlook, being overbearing and creating a sense of enclosure. The application has also failed to demonstrate that there would not be unacceptable harm in respect to reductions in daylight to No. 784 Garratt Lane. Furthermore, the inclusion of windows on the side elevation would lead to unacceptable loss of privacy to adjoining occupiers. The development is therefore contrary to policy LP2 of the Wandsworth Local Plan (2023) and the Housing SPD (2016).",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed development, by reason of its design and layout, would provide substandard accommodation for future occupiers. The proposed dwelling would have insufficient outlook for the habitable bedroom and would fail to provide any private outdoor amenity space. The proposal therefore fails to comply with Policy LP27 of the Wandsworth Local Plan (2023) and Policy D6 of the London Plan (2021).",
    "Reason : 3 - In dealing with this application the Council has implemented the requirement in the National Planning Policy Framework to make available detailed advice in the form of our statutory policies in the Local Plan as well as offering a full pre application advice service. However, we have been unable to seek solutions to problems as the proposal is contrary to our statutory policies and negotiation could not overcome the reasons for refusal.\r\n\r\n"
  ],
